  "raw_text": "38\n\nBan bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto endure, to continue to endure, to continue to stand up to, to remain firm, to remain\nsteadfast\n \n/ aguantar, continuar aguantando, continuar resistiendo, continuar defendiendo, mantenerse firme,\npermanecer firme\n\nBan kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be forever, to live forever, to continue to be, to always be\n \n/ ser para siempre, vivir para siempre,\nseguir siendo, ser siempre\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nAisa yapti nani dîa daukaia sip sa ai luhpia nani ban tânka kasak ra kaia hilp munaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat\ncan parents do in order to help their children to continue to be in the truth?\n \n/ ¿Qué pueden hacer los padres para ayudar a\nsus hijos a seguir en la verdad?)\n\nBan kaia ra\n \n–\n \nfor forever, for always\n \n/ para siempre, eternamente\n\nB\nan kaia\n \nra iwaia\n \n(v\n)\n \n–\n \nto live forever\n \n/ vivir para siempre\n\nBan kaia Kingka\n \n(\n1Timoti 1:17\n)\n \n–\n \nKing of Eternity\n \n/ Rey de la eternidad\n\nRaya ban kaia\n \n(v\n)\n \n–\n \nto be alive forever\n \n/ estar vivo para siempre\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \neverlasting life\n \n/\n \nvida eterna\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka briaia b\nî\nla kaikanka ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe hope of everlasting life\n \n/ la\n\nesperanza de la\n \nvida eterna\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka yabalka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroad to everlasting life\n \n/\n \ncamino a la vida eterna\n\nBan kasak\n \n–\n \nfaithful\n \n/\n \nfiel\n\nBan kra\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nBankra\n)\n \n–\n \nmaybe\n \n/\n \ntal vez\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nMebi\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nBan kra naha taimka ra, ...\n \n–\n \nMaybe at\n \nthis time, ...\n \n/\n \nT\nal vez en este momento,\n \n…\n)\n\nBan kra si\n \n–\n \nmaybe it is the case, maybe it is being the case, maybe so\n \n/ tal vez sea el\n \ncas\no\n, tal vez\n \nsiendo\n\nel caso, tal vez\n\nBan kra talia\n \n–\n \nseems like maybe, possibly\n \n/\n \nparece que tal vez, posiblemente\n\nBan lilia kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto continue to be happy\n \n/ seguir siendo feliz\n\nBan praut kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto continue to be angry, to be holding onto a grudge, to continue to be resentful, to continue\nto be proud\n \n/ continuar enojado, guardar rencor, seguir resentido, seguir orgulloso\n\nBan sakuna\n \n–\n \nnevertheless, in spite of, although, still however, but, however, so, even though\n \n/ sin embargo, a\npesar de, aunque todavía, pero, entonces, aunque, incluso\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKuna\n,\n \nSakuna\n)\n\nBan wina\n \n–\n \nby chance, from nothing, for no reason, suddenly\n \n/ por casualidad, de la nada, sin razón, de repente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-06/20\n):\n \nGâd ra kulkaia lâka ba nahki wan kaina kahbisa ban wina lilka taski nani kaikisa taim?\n \n–\n \nHow does\ngodly fear protect us when by chance we see an impure image?\n \n/ ¿Cómo nos protege el temor de Dios cuando por\ncasualidad vemos una imagen impura?)\n\nBan wina smalkaia\n \n–\n \nInformal witnessing\n \n/ Predicaci\nó\nn informal\n\nBangbang\n \n(a/t:\n \nTibam\n,\n \nTibang\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nrabbit\n \n/ conejo\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nTibang\n \nis more common in Nicaragua than\n \nBangbang\n \n/\n \nTibang\n \nes más común en Nicaragua que\n \nBangbang\n)\n\nBangbang tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhare\n \n/ liebre\n\nBangkaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nBanhkaia\n\nBangkil\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu;\n \nBangel\n-dict-alt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbracelet, bangle\n \n/ pulsera, brazalete\n\n(Note/Nota: Not commonly used.\n \nSee:\n \nMihta lilura\n \n/ No se usa comúnmente.\n \nVer:\n \nMihta lilura\n)\n\nBangwaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nBanhwaia\n\nBanhkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nBahngkaia\n,\n \nBanghkaia\n,\n \nBahnkaia\n,\n \nBangkaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nBanhwaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto fill, to saturate, to\nreplenish, to make full, to bubble, to abound\n \n/ llenar, saturar, reponer, burbujear, abundar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb25\n):\n \nJehova tintka watla... ai prana ni banhkan\n \n–\n \nJehovah... filled the tabernacle with his glory\n \n/ Jehová... llenó el\ntabernáculo con su gloria)\n\nBanhki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make full\n \n/ hacer completo, llenar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Blasi Sturka 1:22\n):\n \nkabu nani ba banhki dauks\n \n–\n \nmake the seas full\n \n/ llena los mares)\n\nBanhki dingkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nUlbi dingkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto fill out and put in\n \n/ llenar y poner\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-12/20\n):\n \nPat luki kaikram ki King Lâka Sturka Smalki nani Skulka ra waia dukiara wauhkataya ba banhki\ndingkaia?\n \n–\n \nHave you already considered filling out and submitting the form for School for Kingdom Evangelizers?\n \n/ Ha\nconsiderado ya completar y enviar el formulario de Escuela para Evangelizadores del Reino?)\n\nBanhki takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become full\n \n/ llenarse\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nbh116\n):\n \nai kyamka sahwi tasba ba bangki takan\n \n–\n \nthe earth became filled with their offspring\n \n/ la tierra se llenó de\nsu descendencia)\n\nSahwi banhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto multiply and fill\n \n/ multiplicar y llenar",
